  ('d0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000065', 'c0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000065', 'b0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003', 'seed', 'voltra-r101', 'Hi Adrián,

E07 is the motor''s overheat protection, not a fault: it cuts power so the motor doesn''t damage itself. On a long climb it triggers when the scooter is working near its limit.

- Use gear 2 rather than 3 on the hill; it draws less current.
- If it trips, give it 10 minutes and it resets on its own.
- Your S2 is on firmware 2.1. Version 2.3.1 fixes early E07 triggers, so please update it in the app first.

If you still see E07 on flat ground after the update, tell me and we''ll look at the controller.

Dani, Voltra Support', now() - interval '41657 minutes'),
